<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baghdadi Jews</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baghdadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were communities of Arabic-speaking Jews from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and neighbouring lands who settled in the trading ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> from the late 18th century. Their main centres were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>, and leading families such as the Sassoons built great commercial and industrial fortunes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, opium, shipping and banking.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdadi-jews.jpg" alt="Baghdadi Jews" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer, mid-19th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_Sassoon_and_sons.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
